UPDATING; delete DELETING
follow-up: create=GetWorkRequest -> GetDrPlan;
update=GetWorkRequest -> GetDrPlan;
delete=GetDrPlan/ListDrPlans confirm-delete
supported drift: definedTags, displayName,
freeformTags, planGroups
reject before mutate: force-new fields
drProtectionGroupId, sourcePlanId, type
create-only fields: none
list lookup: oci_disaster_recovery_dr_plans
filters drProtectionGroupId, displayName, type,
drPlanId; exact drProtectionGroupId plus
displayName and type unique match; tracked
rereads and delete confirmation can additionally
narrow by drPlanId
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
DrPlan create and update are work-request-backed
and resume through status.async.current as the
canonical in-flight tracker.
List responses expose DrPlanSummary items only,
so the runtime rereads GetDrPlan before status
projection or mutable drift checks that depend
on planGroups or sourcePlanId.
Create ignores spec.planGroups because
CreateDrPlanDetails does not accept planGroups;
in-place plan group edits are published only
through UpdateDrPlanDetails.
The resource-local update builder strips
read-only group and step fields from GetDrPlan
before diffing so service-owned metadata does
not cause perpetual updates.
Refresh, verify, plan execution, and other
disaster recovery helper families remain out of
scope for this controller-backed runtime.
end note
